{"title":"More optimistic results on AI and job markets","link":"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/~/968480747/0/marginalrevolution~More-optimistic-results-on-AI-and-job-markets.html","date":1788246339000,"content":"<p>Here is <a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/~/t/0/0/marginalrevolution/~https://x.com/Jon_Hartley_/status/2094553387316453458?s=20\" target=\"_blank\">a good Jon Hartley thread</a>.  Here is<a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/~/t/0/0/marginalrevolution/~https://papers.ssrn.com/sol3/papers.cfm?abstract_id=5136877&amp;__cf_chl_tk=2WJamtftqdfDIR9yFfYIrEBu9TugTrmIRI0Zik5sUPs-1788228368-1.0.1.1-v8szdkEGHn_fabviS.7NDaGxeVc7tIE1ievCc8_1tx8\" target=\"_blank\"> the paper</a>, with Jolevski, Melo, and Moore.  From Jon’s thread: “Generative AI adoption is widespread, but substantial aggregate labor-market disruption is not yet visible. Workers nevertheless perceive substantial displacement risk, especially when firsthand use reveals that AI can perform key tasks for their job.”  And again here is <a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/~/t/0/0/marginalrevolution/~https://marginalrevolution.com/marginalrevolution/2026/08/ai-and-employment-what-the-firms-say.html\" target=\"_blank\">Alex’s post from yesterday</a>.</p>\r\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/~/t/0/0/marginalrevolution/~https://marginalrevolution.com/marginalrevolution/2026/09/more-optimistic-results-on-ai-and-job-markets.html\">More optimistic results on AI and job markets</a> appeared first on <a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/~/t/0/0/marginalrevolution/~https://marginalrevolution.com\">Marginal REVOLUTION</a>.</p>\r\n<img height=\"1\" width=\"1\" src=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/~/i/968480747/0/marginalrevolution\" />\r\n<div><a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/_/28/968480747/marginalrevolution\"><img height=\"20\" src=\"https://assets.feedblitz.com/i/fblike20.png\" /></a> <a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/_/29/968480747/marginalrevolution,\"><img height=\"20\" src=\"https://